course: dictionary
lesson: 14940
title: Using a word in your own words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Regurgitate means to bring swallowed food back up into your mouth. It is a verb, so you can say he regurgitates, she regurgitated, or they are regurgitating. It is a long word, so break it into chunks: re-gur-gi-tate.
explain: «The baby bird waited with its beak open while its mum regurgitated a meal of worms.» The clues are baby bird, beak open and meal of worms. The mum is not eating again. She is bringing food up to give to her chick, so here the word means bringing swallowed food back up on purpose.
explain: «Our teacher said, "Don't just regurgitate facts in the test. Tell me what they mean in your own words."» This time the word means something different. It means repeating facts word for word without really understanding them. The clue is "in your own words", which is the opposite of repeating. Always check the words around the word.
fact: Regurgitate means to bring swallowed food back up into the mouth.
fact: Some animals, like birds and wolves, regurgitate food on purpose to feed their babies.
fact: Cows bring up cud to chew again, and owls regurgitate pellets of bones and fur.
fact: In school, to regurgitate facts means to repeat them word for word without understanding them.
fact: «Regurgitation» is the noun, the name for the act of regurgitating.
exercise: «The baby bird waited while its mum regurgitated a meal for it.» What does regurgitated mean here? | Hid the food under a leaf | Ate the food very quickly | Flew away to find a nest | *Brought swallowed food back up for her chick
exercise: «Owls regurgitate pellets of bones and fur.» What comes back up in a pellet? | *Bones and fur that the owl cannot digest | Sweet juice from flowers | Seeds from a fruit tree | Eggs laid in a nest
exercise: Ella says, «Don't just regurgitate facts in the exam.» What does she want you to do? | *Explain the facts in your own words | Forget all the facts you have learnt | Repeat the facts word for word without thinking | Write the facts in bigger letters
test: «After eating too fast, the puppy regurgitated its dinner onto the carpet.» What does regurgitated mean? | Hid under the sofa | Barked very loudly | Licked the carpet clean | *Brought swallowed food back up
test: Which pupil is regurgitating facts? | Priya asks a question when she is confused | Sam draws a labelled diagram of the heart | Maya explains the water cycle in her own words | *Ravi copies the textbook definition word for word and cannot explain it
exam: Which is the best meaning of regurgitate? | Cook food until it is soft | *Bring swallowed food back up into the mouth | Give your food away to a friend | Swallow food very slowly
